   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "3. In Vietnam the message became a war program, and the agency's own research said the message was not the problem (1964-1967)",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "From 1964 USIA took over the Saigon government's information effort and the American psychological-warfare effort. The Director called it the weakest part of the war; a field reviewer blamed Vietnamese motivation; USIA's survey in Long An found apathy produced by insecurity and ineffective government; and by 1967 an internal review argued the agency had taken on tasks outside its sphere."
